# A Visual Basic form resource is binary. Git must not touch its line endings.
#
# This is not a preference. `corpus/vb6-code/Hidden-Markov-model/frmHMM.frx`
# arrived from upstream with one byte missing: its record header declares 56
# bytes of payload and only 55 are present, and the file ends with a lone 0x0A
# where a 0x0D 0x0A pair belongs. A carriage return was stripped by end of line
# normalisation. Upstream marks these files `-diff`, which suppresses the diff
# but does not stop normalisation.
*.frx binary
*.ctx binary
*.dsx binary

# Executables and the other compiled artifacts in the corpus.
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.ocx binary

# Visual Basic source is text that VB6 writes with CRLF. Keep it exactly as the
# compiler and the IDE produced it, because the differential gate compares it
# against bytes recovered from a binary.
*.frm -text
*.bas -text
*.cls -text
*.ctl -text
*.vbp -text
*.vbw -text
*.mak -text
